llvm-4.0.0 backport patch: block placement keeps 3.9's forward check (PS4)

This patch CHANGES CODE GENERATION in MachineBlockPlacement's
hasBetterLayoutPredecessor. r277187 (Kyle Butt, llvm-project 02d8d054abaa,
2016-07-29, first release LLVM 4.0) replaced the three lines of 3.9's
forward check there; this patch restores them (the commit's comments are
left). D51 held this reversal for a second witness; round 212B's
whole-module measurement gives the missing support: 0x12fd360 is equal to
the base in the prebuilt 3.7.1's module. With the patch that function
compiles to the base's bytes, two functions of the module change and no
matched game row changes (round 214B; the supervisor's sweep of the five
patches of D66 to D70 together). The rule has no byte form to census.

diff -ru a/lib/CodeGen/MachineBlockPlacement.cpp b/lib/CodeGen/MachineBlockPlacement.cpp
--- a/lib/CodeGen/MachineBlockPlacement.cpp
+++ b/lib/CodeGen/MachineBlockPlacement.cpp
@@ -748,6 +748,11 @@
   // but they all fit this general pattern.)
   BranchProbability HotProb = getLayoutSuccessorProbThreshold(BB);
 
+  // PS4: LLVM 3.9's forward check (removed by r277187, 02d8d054abaa, first in 4.0): a
+  // successor below the hot probability is laid out in topological order.
+  if (SuccProb < HotProb)
+    return true;
+
   // Make sure that a hot successor doesn't have a globally more
   // important predecessor.
   BlockFrequency CandidateEdgeFreq = MBFI->getBlockFreq(BB) * RealSuccProb;
